<p class="copy">
	Trucks are small cargo vessels, often little more than a pilot's cabin and thrusters bolted to a cargo hold. Used to transport goods around a station, between ships, and even from planetary surfaces to orbit, trucks are the workhorses of spaceborne commerce. Truck cargo is most often secured in standardized, pressure-sealed shipping containers, with the pilot rarely knowing anything about what's inside.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	Trucks range in size from single-cab haulers to miles-long trains of interconnected containers, bookended by trucks large enough to serve as <?php echo sf_lore_link('tugs', 'tugs'); ?> in their own right. Whatever their size, crew accommodations are usually an afterthought, with the space and systems that would be devoted to passengers instead given over to engines, cargo, and the equipment needed to move them.
</p>
